# The queue consumers this repository runs, one line each.
#
# This is the only place a consumer is written by hand. `make consumers` makes
# the rest from it: the Deployments in k8s/base/jobs/consumers.yaml, the consumer
# services in docker-compose.yaml and docker-compose.dev.yaml, and
# MAGENTO_CONSUMERS in k8s/base/config/env/common.env. `make verify-consumers`
# and `make check` refuse any of those that no longer match this file.
#
# A line is the queue's name, then any of the settings below, then `#` and what
# the consumer is for. That sentence becomes the comment above its Deployment.
#
#   max=N              messages before the process restarts itself (default 100)
#   memory=REQ/LIMIT   the Deployment's memory request and limit (default 192Mi/384Mi)
#   name=NAME          the Deployment's name, where the one made from the queue's
#                      name will not do. Never change the name of a consumer that
#                      is running: the cluster would keep the old Deployment
#                      consuming beside the new one.
#   compose=NAME       the Compose service's name, where it differs from the Deployment's
#
# WHY THESE EIGHT. With cron_run false a consumer not named here never runs, and
# its messages wait with no error, so a queue belongs here once a store does the
# work that feeds it. The first six are fed by work in the admin or on the
# catalog: a bulk API call, a mass attribute update, a product's SKU changed, a
# product deleted or imported, the media gallery's sync, and coupon codes
# generated in bulk. The last two are fed by every order. Magento declares more
# than these; docs/configuration.md says how to see them all.
#
# TO ADD ONE, add its line and run `make consumers`. The queue's name alone is
# a whole line. Every store this copy of the repository runs gets the consumer,
# so a queue that only one of several stores has does not belong here.

async.operations.all             memory=384Mi/768Mi  compose=consumer-async-operations          # Bulk and asynchronous REST API calls. The heaviest consumer here by a wide margin.
product_action_attribute.update  memory=256Mi/512Mi  compose=consumer-product-action-attribute  # Mass attribute updates from the admin product grid.
inventory.reservations.update    max=500                                                        # Moves a product's MSI reservations to its new SKU when the SKU is changed.
inventory.reservations.cleanup   max=500                                                        # Deletes the MSI reservations of products that were deleted, or removed by an import.
media.gallery.synchronization    memory=256Mi/512Mi                                             # Records the files under pub/media in the media gallery's tables, read through the shared claim from ADR-003.
codegeneratorProcessor           name=consumer-codegenerator                                    # Generates coupon codes in bulk for a cart price rule, from the admin.
inventory.reservations.updateSalabilityStatus  name=consumer-inventory-salability-status   # After an order's reservations, refreshes whether each product is still salable.
sales.rule.update.coupon.usage                                                             # Counts a cart price rule's uses after an order; coupon and customer counts are kept without it.
